                                            "summary":  "Ron Baron\u0027s mutual funds have delivered estimated returns exceeding $60 billion since the early 1980s, outperforming peers and major indices across decades. A disproportionate share of those gains came from early, concentrated positions in Tesla and SpaceX. Baron\u0027s philosophy centers on long-term conviction, holding exceptional businesses through volatility, and ignoring the position-sizing and universe constraints that govern most institutional investors.",
